# ==========================================================================
# quran-clips — track the CREATION PROCESS, not the output.
# Tracked: qc/, scripts/, templates/, .claude/, assets/ (fonts + scene images),
#          style/**/*.md specs + fx code, docs/ (README demos), and the FIVE
#          example clip.yaml recipes the golden tests and the README refer to.
# Ignored: downloaded footage, exported reels, per-clip renders, the venv, and
#          the working library under clips/ (that is my own output, not code).
# ==========================================================================

# --- Downloaded / exported / recreatable trees -----------------------------
# downloaded YouTube source videos + subtitles (re-downloadable).
# EXCEPT sources/meta/: one small yaml per video (title, duration, fps,
# dimensions, uploader) written by `qc source add`. That is derived knowledge
# we paid a network round-trip for and that `qc locate` reads, so it must
# survive a clean checkout even though the .mp4 next to it does not.
# Git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so the exclusion has to be
# `sources/*` (contents) rather than `sources/` for the negation to be
# reachable at all.
sources/*
!sources/meta/
# exported final reels (regenerable from clip.yaml)
reels/
# python venv for ASR (recreate with pip install)
tools/

# --- The clip library -------------------------------------------------------
# clips/ is the working library: authoring folders, renders, Finder aliases and
# per-clip posting state. None of it is needed to run the pipeline, so the whole
# tree is local-only, with an explicit keep list at the bottom of this file for
# the handful of clip.yaml recipes that ship as examples / golden-test inputs.
# tags.yaml is posting state (posted?, keyword tags) and never ships.
# Git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so the clip folders are
# re-admitted (`!clips/*/`) and their CONTENTS excluded instead, which is what
# makes the per-file keeps at the bottom reachable.
clips/*
!clips/*/
clips/*/*

# --- Media, anywhere --------------------------------------------------------
*.mp4
*.mov
*.wav
*.m4a

# --- Reference frames / QA stills (extracted or rendered, regenerable) ------
style/**/*.jpg
style/**/*.jpeg
style/**/*.png

# --- Generated reports ------------------------------------------------------
pipeline-review.html

# --- Python / OS cruft ------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.DS_Store

# ===========================================================================
# Explicit keeps — these are INPUTS to the pipeline, never outputs.
# (Defensive negations: nothing above should swallow them.)
# ===========================================================================
!scripts/
!templates/
!.claude/
!assets/
!assets/fonts/*.ttf
!assets/reciters/*.png
!style/**/*.md
!*.excalidraw

# The example recipes, and ONLY these: al-ahzab-56-56 is the `default`-style
# clip embedded in the README; the other four are the inputs the golden
# fixtures under tests/golden/ were recorded against (at-tawbah-128-128 is
# also the README's `bars` clip). Every other clip folder stays local.
!clips/al-ahzab-56-56/clip.yaml
!clips/al-ahzab-70-71/clip.yaml
!clips/al-anam-102-103/clip.yaml
!clips/al-infitar-6-9/clip.yaml
!clips/at-tawbah-128-128/clip.yaml

# README demo videos — the one place an .mp4 is tracked on purpose.
!docs/*.mp4
